# Complaint to the California Attorney General: Anthropic PBC and the Generative AI Training Data Transparency Act

Avik Jain

Part A is the formal complaint under California Civil Code sections 3110–3111 and Business and Professions Code section 17200, prepared for submission via https://oag.ca.gov/contact/consumer-complaint-against-business-or-company or by mail to Public Inquiry Unit, Office of the Attorney General, P.O. Box 944255, Sacramento, CA 94244-2550 [S1]. Part B is the accompanying California Consumer Privacy Act request to Anthropic PBC. Part C sets out proposed Civil Code section 3111.5 mandating public disclosure of post-training preference records for systems offered to answer questions of fact and public affairs. Part D lists the filing exhibits and pre-filing verification items. Every statement of fact is cited in Part E.

