### 8. Parallel complaint against OpenAI OpCo, LLC

Because the Attorney General's intake form accepts one business per submission, a parallel complaint is filed separately against OpenAI OpCo, LLC, 1455 3rd Street, San Francisco, CA 94158, the contracting party to OpenAI's consumer terms [S21], with sections 3 and 5 replaced by the following.

OpenAI's "Training Data Summary Pursuant to California Civil Code Section 3111" is a short narrative [S19]. It says OpenAI develops its systems using publicly available data, data accessed through third parties, "and information that our users or human trainers and researchers provide or generate", that it also uses synthetic data, and that its datasets contain "trillions of tokens" of text, image, audio and audiovisual content [S19]. On the data its human trainers produce it gives no label types, no counts, no collection periods and no account of how those datasets were processed, though section 3111 asks each of these [S2]. OpenAI's help center shows the page as recently updated; the filing attaches the version current on the filing date alongside any archived version from 1 January 2026 so that post-release modifications can be compared directly.

